-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",413,{
[13185]="7001752C\n1\tDefeat howling overseers in the Dark Delvings (total: 6)\030Defeat snarling overseers in the Dark Delvings (total: 6)\030Defeat Dark-maw masters in the Dark Delving (total: 8)\030Defeated dark world-eaters in the Dark Delving (total: 4)\tThe Dark Delvings lie far to the south-east of the Shadowed Refuge. Moggi made mention of lamps placed in the Dark Delvings by the dwarves and how they may drive back some of the Nameless, but he thinks that there are others who are unafraid of such Light. Use caution as you fulfill this task.\n2\tTalk to Moggi at the Shadowed Refuge\tMoggi is at the Shadowed Refuge, far to the north-west of the Dark Delving. You fought your way into the Dark Delving and there defeated many of the nameless horrors. You should now return to the Shadowed Refuge and inform Moggi of your success.\n",
[13186]="7000007B\n1\tFind the missing third gear\tThe third gear is in a chest in the ruins of an ancient crypt in Emyn Hoedh, the barrow-mounds in Haudh Lin, north-east of Gondamon. Bávor has asked you to recover the third missing gear for the Vault of the Mountain. He warned you of rumours regarding the presence of barrow-wights amongst the old mounds.\n2\tBring the third gear to Bávor\tBávor is in Thorin's Hall. Bávor will be pleased to begin working with the third gear.\n",
[13187]="700572F8\n1\tInspect the illusion of the third stone\tAn illusion has appeared before you in the Crown Chamber. You should inspect the illusion of the third stone.\n2\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n3\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n4\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n5\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n6\tInspect the illusion of the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n7\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n8\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n9\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n10\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n11\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n12\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n13\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n14\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n15\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n16\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n17\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n18\tFind the third stone.\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n19\tFind the third stone.\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n20\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n21\tFind the third stone\tThe missing stone is out there somewhere, waiting to be found.\n22\tFind the third stone somewhere in Angmar\tThe missing stone was found by Mordirith, and must be somewhere in Angmar.\n23\tReturn the stone to its pedestal\tYou have found one of the missing stones! You should return it to its rightful place in the Crown Chamber.\n",
[13188]="700077EA\n1\tDefeat Midgewater sappers in the Midgewater Marsh (total: 8)\tGoblin-sappers have infiltrated the southern expanse of the Midgewater Marshes. Bill Mossfoot has tasked you with defeating the Midgewater sappers before they can take their deadly burning oil to Staddle.\n2\tTalk to Bill Mossfoot\tBill Mossfoot is at his camp in the Midgewater Marsh to the south-east of the Midgewater Ruins. News of your success against the goblin-sappers should relieve Bill Mossfoot of some of his worries.\n",
[13189]="7003EB09\n1\tDefeat boars in the South Trollshaws (total: 8)\tThere are boars dwelling in the South Trollshaws. While you are in the South Trollshaws, you should cull the number of boars, perhaps lessening the threat they present to travellers upon the road.\n",
[13190]="7003EA7C\n1\tSearch for Orofarnë's seed\030Search for Lassemista's seed\030Search for Carnimírië's seed\tThe seeds of Orofarnë, Lassemista, and Carnimírië can be found along the borders of Nan Curunír and Fangorn Forest. Quickbeam wants you find the seeds of his fallen friends in Nan Curunír so he can honour their memory.\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam can be found to the east of Isengard in Nan Curunír. You have recovered all three seeds from Nan Curunír and should now return them to Quickbeam's keeping.\n3\tPlant Lassemista's seed at the base of Orthanc\tA good spot to plant Lassemista's seed can be found at the southern base of Orthanc. Quickbeam has asked that you plant Lassemista's seed outside Orthanc to spite Saruman and bring forth new life in Nan Curunír.\n4\tTalk to Quickbeam at Derndingle The Huorn outside Isengard can guide you to Derndingle\tQuickbeam can be found at Derndingle in Fangorn Forest, which can be reached with the aid of the Huorn outside Isengard. You have planted Lassemista's seed at the base of Orthanc, and should now meet Quickbeam in Fangorn Forest.\n",
[13191]="700428C7\n1\tDefeated scouts ([see journal]/3)\tKeep scouts from blowing their horns three times. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[13192]="7002F980\n1\tDefeat mounted Orcs in the western farmlands (total: 10)\tThe abandoned farms can be found south and west of Cliving. Many of the mounted Orc-forces have continued to occupy and defile the abandoned farms.\n2\tTalk to Captain Garmund outside of Cliving\tCaptain Garmund can be found at the western watch-tower just west of Cliving. Captain Garmund will be pleased to see your actions dealing with the Orc-invaders.\n",
[13193]="7005A956\n1\tCollect copper ore (total: 8)\030Collect marble (total: 6)\030Collect amethyst (total: 4)\tThe three types of stone Rísti Graver seeks can be found in Máttugard. You should collect copper, marble, and amethyst for Rísti Graver.\n2\tRepair the Throne of Zidir-nesad with copper ore\tThe Throne of Zidir-nesad can be found at the Steepset in Máttugard. You should repair the Throne of Zidir-nesad under Rísti Graver's supervision.\n3\tRepair the Throne of Zidir-nesad with the marble\tThe Throne of Zidir-nesad can be found at the Steepset in Máttugard. You should repair the Throne of Zidir-nesad under Rísti Graver's supervision.\n4\tRepair the Throne of Zidir-nesad with the amethyst\tThe Throne of Zidir-nesad can be found at the Steepset in Máttugard. You should repair the Throne of Zidir-nesad under Rísti Graver's supervision.\n5\tTalk to Rísti Graver\tRísti Graver can be found at the Steepset in Máttugard. You should talk to Rísti Graver.\n",
[13194]="7005B5EA\n1\tSpeak to Mother Amma\tMother Amma is in Stókkset, in south-west Clovengap. You should talk to Mother Amma.\n",
[13195]="7000E5BA\n1\tTalk to Kaj\tKaj is in Pynti-peldot. You should speak with Kaj when you are ready to assist him with his ritual.\n2\tTalk to Pinja\tPinja is outside her house at Lumi-talletta, south-west of Pynti-peldot in Itä-ma. You should speak with Pinja at once.\n",
[13196]="7000135F\n1\tBring the nightshade-plants back to Oflár\030Collect nightshade-plants (total: 6)\tThe nightshade plant grows north and east of Maethad, to the south-east of Myrkworth. Oflár has asked you to collect Nightshade plants to prepare a tincture that he hopes will prove useful against the wights of Imlad Balchorth.\n",
[13197]="7005AAFD\n1\tFind Klúso near Bazan-medan\tHórin thinks the best course of action is to continue higher into the Welkin-lofts in search of Ausma's apprentices. You should continue south and find Klúso.\n2\tTalk to Klúso near Bazan-medan\tKlúso can be found near Bazan-medan. You should talk to Klúso.\n3\tTalk to Klúso and hear his report\tKlúso is ready to give his scouting report. You should talk to Klúso and complete 'Instance: The Tipping Point'.\n4\tTalk to Klúso near Bazan-medan\tKlúso can be found west of Bazan-medan. You should talk to Klúso.\n5\tTalk to Hórin near Bazan-medan\tHórin can be found next to Klúso, west of Bazan-medan. You should talk to Hórin.\n6\tComplete 'Three Faction Battle!' for Klúso\030Complete 'The Unyielding and the Overwhelming' for Klúso\030Call Hórin and help him with 'Caught In The Middle'\tA battle between the Orcs and hobgoblins has erupted in the ice-giant settlement of Thyrstáth. You should complete objectives in Thyrstáth for both Klúso and Hórin.\n7\tCall Hórin and talk to him\tYou should talk to Hórin. Use the summoning horn to call Hórin to your side.\n8\tFind the door to the main keep in south-east Thyrstáth\tYou have defeated the Orcs and hobgoblins, and possibly earned some favour with the ice-giants. You should find the door to the main keep, in the south-eastern reaches of Thyrstáth.\n9\tCall Hórin and talk to him\tYou should talk to Hórin. Use the summoning horn to call Hórin to your side.\n",
[13198]="70045271\n1\tFind the tomb at Halifirien\tGuthláf has asked you to visit the tomb at Halifirien in the Beacon Hills, and take note of what you see.\n2\tDefeat the tomb robbers (total: 8)\030Defeat the tomb robbers at the tomb\tDefend the tomb at Halifirien.\n3\tReturn to Guthláf\tYou should return to Guthláf and tell him how you saw the tomb at Halifirien and defended it from pillagers.\n",
[13199]="700097E3\n1\tTalk to Calenglad and travel to the tomb of Elendil\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on Tinnudir, in Evendim. Calenglad is waiting to speak with you about travelling to the tomb of Elendil to reclaim the Silithar for Aragorn.\n2\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on Tinnudir, in Evendim. Calenglad is waiting for you to speak with him about your adventures in the tomb of Elendil.\n",
[13200]="70059352\n1\tSearch Addy's chest of personal belongings\030Search Nye's chest of personal belongings\tChests with the personal belongings of Addy Rushtuft and Nye Crowfoot can be found at Trader's Wharf. You should search the chests belonging to Addy Rushtuft and Nye Crowfoot.\n2\tTalk to Enid Nettlesting\tEnid Nettlesting can be found at Trader's Wharf. You should talk to Enid Nettlesting.\n3\tTalk to Enid Nettlesting in Writhenset\tEnid Nettlesting wishes to go to Writhenset to get to the bottom of things. You should talk to Enid Nettlesting in Writhenset.\n4\tEnter the tomb\tThe entrance to Haudh Eglan can be found in Writhenset. You should enter Haudh Eglan.\n5\tDefeat tomb-robbers and recover stolen relics (total: 6)\030Defeat Addy Rushtuft\030Defeat Nye Crowfoot\tThe tomb-robbers can be found in Haudh Eglan. You should defeat the tomb-robbers and recover what they have already pilfered.\n6\tPlace the relics back into the ceremonial coffer\tThe ceremonial coffer can be found in Haudh Eglan. You should return the relics to their proper place in the tomb.\n7\tTalk to Enid Nettlesting in Writhenset\tEnid Nettlesting can be found in Writhenset. You should talk to Enid Nettlesting in Writhenset.\n8\tTalk to Enid Nettlesting at Trader's Wharf\tEnid Nettlesting wishes to return to Trader's Wharf. You should talk to Enid Nettlesting at Trader's Wharf.\n",
[13201]="7005AAAA\n1\tFind Kyrstig\tKyrstig should be scouting somewhere near Adkhât-zahhar, the Houses of Rest, on the western side of the Pit of Stonejaws. You should find Kyrstig.\n2\tComplete 'Wights Within'\030Complete 'Tombs of the Old Lords'\030Complete 'Angmarim in Akhaldarâg'\030Complete 'Dangerous Dwarf-eaters'\030Find information about Loknashra\tKyrstig has discovered that the Angmarim are desecrating the Houses of Rest. You should help Krystig with quests in Akhaldarâg.\n3\tTalk to Kyrstig\tKyrstig is near Akhaldarâg, north west of Bárgstad. You should talk to Kyrstig.\n",
[13202]="70007377\n1\tFind Odo Pipes\tOdo Pipes is hiding somewhere in Michel Delving. Rollo Newbuck has sent you to find Odo Pipes, rumoured to be the best Hider in the Shire. Odo is hiding somewhere in Michel Delving. Rollo thinks that Daisy or Polo, in their usual hiding-places, might have some clue to Odo's location.\n2\tTalk to Rollo Newbuck\tRollo Newbuck is east of The Bird and Baby Inn, within the stone wall around Town Hole. Rollo is waiting to hear that you have found Odo Pipes and his hiding-place.\n",
[13203]="7004D4A9\n1\tDefeat spiders in Torech Emel\tTorech Emel is found in the north-western reach of Eryn Lasgalen. You should defeat any spiders you come across in Torech Emel.\n2\tDefeat spiders in Torech Emel (total: 12)\tTorech Emel is found in the north-western part of Eryn Lasgalen. You should defeat any spiders you come across in Torech Emel.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many spiders in Torech Emel.\n",
[13204]="70030F65\n1\tObtain a war-steed by helping Langhold\tYou may not obtain a war-steed until you finish assisting the town of Langhold. To begin the lesson, you must first obtain a war-steed.\n2\tComplete the riding course upon the tourney field\tSpeak with Seoca at the tourney field directly south of Harwick.\n3\tSpeak to Seoca at the Tourney Field\tSpeak with Seoca to complete your war-steed training.\n4\tSpeak with Anmar at the Harwick Mead-hall\tSpeak with Anmar, guard at the Mead-hall of Harwick in the Wold.\n",
[13205]="70030F74\n1\tSpeak with Seoca\tBegin your instruction in how to ride a war-steed by speaking with Seoca.\n2\tMount your war-steed near the outer starting line\tMount your war-steed near the outer track starting line.\n3\tLaps completed ([see journal]/2)\tFollow the direction of Seoca as you circle the tourney field and learn to control your steed. You must make two full circuits of the outer track in order to proceed.\n4\tSpeak with Seoca\tSpeak with Seoca.\n5\tBlue flags passed ([see journal]/6)\tRun the flags course as directed by Seoca. On the first round, you must pass through the blue flags. On the second round, you must pass through the red flags. On the third round, you must pass through both sets of flags at once. Tip: This course is not timed, but if you miss a flag, the flag count will restart on your next lap. Tip: If you find the flags are too closely spaced to pass through at full speed, try slowing down a little. Tip: Using the mouse to turn allows finer control than the the keyboard.\n6\tRed flags passed ([see journal]/5)\tRun the flags course as directed by Seoca. On the first round, you must pass through the blue flags. On the second round, you must pass through the red flags. On the third round, you must pass through both sets of flags at once. - Tip: This course is not timed, but if you miss a flag, the flag count will restart on your next lap. - Tip: If you find the flags are too closely spaced to pass through at full speed, try slowing down a little. - Tip: Using the mouse to turn allows finer control than the the keyboard.\n7\tAll flags passed ([see journal]/11)\tRun the flags course as directed by Seoca. On the first round, you must pass through the blue flags. On the second round, you must pass through the red flags. On the third round, you must pass through both sets of flags at once. Important: This course is not timed, but if you miss a flag, the flag count will restart on your next lap. Tip: If you find the flags are too closely spaced to pass through at full speed, try slowing down a little. Tip: Using the mouse to turn allows finer control than the the keyboard.\n8\tSpeak with Seoca\tSpeak with Seoca to begin the next training course.\n9\tFences jumped ([see journal]/4)\tJump each of the fences as you ride around the track. If you miss a fence, your count will reset when you cross the start line and you can keep going.\n10\tFences jumped ([see journal]/6)\tJump each of the fences as you ride around the track. If you miss a fence, your count will reset when you cross the start line and you can keep going.\n11\tSpeak with Seoca\tSpeak with Seoca near the jousting course in the middle of the field.\n12\tBlows landed ([see journal]/10)\tThis is the combat skill course. Ride back and forth between the target dummies at either end of the field, striking each in turn. - Tip: Queue your attacks before you reach your target. - Tip: Slowing down before a turn allows you to turn much faster.\n13\tSpeak with Seoca\tSpeak with Seoca to complete your training.\n",
[13206]="70027177\n1\tSearch crates near Hen Turrau (total: 5)\tCrates can be found around Hen Turrau, east of Barnavon. You should search the crates left at Hen Turrau for further evidence of Saruman's interference.\n2\tDefeat Ox-clan sentries at Hen Turrau (total: 2)\tDunlending guards can be found at Hen Turrau. You should defeat the Dunlending guards that have arrived to garrison the watch-tower.\n3\tBring the weapons to Gwilum in Barnavon\tGwilum is at Barnavon, far to the west of Hen Turrau. You should report what you have found to Gwilum.\n",
[13207]="7002F919\n1\tInfiltrate the Gondorian tower and defeat the leader of the Orc forces\tMinas Rant is west of Springview Estate, at the edge of the stream that runs across the Norcrofts. Cyneswith believes that the commander of the Orcs inhabiting the farmsteads has likely established his base within the Gondorian tower of Minas Rant.\n2\tSpeak to Cyneswith\tCyneswith awaits at the Springview Estate to the east of Minas Rant. Cyneswith is eager to hear of your stirke against the commander of the invading Orc forces.\n",
[13208]="7001EE04\n1\tDefeat corpses in Sammath Gûl (total: 40)\tThe corpses are scattered throughout Sammath Gûl in Dol Guldur. The Malledhrim have asked you to scour the reeking halls of Sammath Gûl by destroying the corpses that litter the tower.\n",
[13209]="70047AE4\n1\tDefeat Uruks within the Towers of the Teeth (total: 12)\tYou should defeat Uruk-hai within the Towers of the Teeth.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many Uruks within the Towers of the Teeth.\n",
[13210]="70025A19\n1\tSearch for Ivar's minions in Stoneheight\tSearch through the town for the leaders of the mercenary minions who still remain in Stoneheight.\n2\tDefeat Gundúl\tGundúl is one of the minions of the Gaunt-lord Ivar who remain behind in the village of Stoneheight. Defeat him and put an end to the evil caused by the goblin mercenaries.\n3\tSearch for more of Ivar's minions\tSearch through the remnants of the town for the commanders of the sellsword rebels.\n4\tDefeat Búbhosh-grat\tBúbhosh-grat is yet another of the minions of Ivar at Stoneheight. This uruk-hai must be defeated in order to drive the bandits from the village.\n5\tDiscover the location of the sellsword leader\tThe leader of Ivar's sellswords has yet to be seen. This man must be overcome to end the occupation of Stoneheight.\n6\tDale Truitt is the last of the sellswords in the service of Ivar. You must remove the mercenary leader to free Stoneheight from the grip of the vandals.\t\n",
[13211]="70044497\n1\tDefeat enemies of Rohan in the Wold (total: 6)\030Defeat enemies of Rohan in the Norcrofts (total: 6)\tBingo wants to travel to the town of Cliving, in the Norcrofts of East Rohan, and has asked you to defeat the enemies of Rohan in the Wold and the Norcrofts as you journey.\n2\tTalk to Bingo outside the entrance to Cliving, in the Norcrofts\tBingo is outside the entrance to the town of Cliving in the Norcrofts, in East Rohan.\n3\tLearn what is wrong with Willem Whisker\tWillem Whisker is outside the entrance to the town of Cliving in the Norcrofts, in East Rohan.\n4\tTalk to Bingo outside the entrance to Cliving, in the Norcrofts\tBingo is outside the entrance to the town of Cliving in the Norcrofts, in East Rohan.\n5\tWalk to the entrance of the Mead Hall in Cliving\tThe Mead Hall of Cliving is in the north-east corner of the town. Bingo wants to walk to the Mead Hall of Cliving and learn the situation for adventurers in the Norcrofts.\n6\tTalk to Egwylf outside the Mead Hall of Cliving\tEgwylf is outside the Mead Hall of Cliving, in the Norcrofts.\n7\tTalk to Bingo outside the Mead Hall of Cliving\tBingo is outside the Mead Hall of Cliving, in the Norcrofts.\n8\tFind some sign that the agents of the Blood Eye are in Cliving\tAgents of the Cult of the Blood Eye may have come to the town of Cliving, in the Norcrofts. Egwylf asked you to search the town of Cliving for any sign of the agents of the Blood Eye.\n9\tPick up the Blood Eye brooch from behind the tents\tYou found a brooch with a red gem on a log behind some tents in the eastern reaches of Cliving, and should pick it up.\n10\tBring the Blood Eye brooch to Egwylf outside the Mead Hall of Cliving\tEgwylf is outside the Mead Hall of Cliving, in the Norcrofts. You found a brooch with a red gem abandoned in a corner of Cliving, behind some tents.\n11\tTalk to Bingo outside the Mead Hall of Cliving\tBingo is outside the Mead Hall of Cliving, in the Norcrofts.\n",
[13212]="7005466C\n1\tFind the mysterious footprints\tThe mysterious footprints of which the Rangers spoke can be found north-west of Echad Taerdim. You should find the footprints with Legolas.\n2\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas would like to talk to you about these strange footprints. You should talk to Legolas.\n3\tFind the Ungoledain\tYou have discovered evidence of an Ungoledain presence in Cirith Ungol. You should follow the tracks to find the Ungoledain.\n4\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas would like to speak to you about the Ungoledain camp you discovered. You should talk to Legolas.\n5\tAttempt to take an Ungoladan prisoner\tYou have discovered an Ungoledain camp within Cirith Ungol. Legolas has decided a prisoner may yield some useful information. You should attempt to take an Ungoladan prisoner within Cadar Skûs.\n6\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas would like to speak with you. You should talk to Legolas.\n7\tFind a safe place to regroup near Cadar Skûs\tLegolas would like to regroup in a safer location. You should find a safer spot to talk south of Cadar Skûs.\n8\tDefeat the attacker!\tYou are being ambushed! Defeat the attacker!\n9\tTalk to Legolas\tThe Ungoladan attacker has been defeated. You should talk to Legolas.\n",
[13213]="70045270\n1\tCover Rohirrim tracks (total: 12)\tHelp Déorwine's scouts and cover any tracks left by the Rohirrim in the Beacon Hills.\n2\tReturn to Déorwine\tReturn to Déorwine in the camp in Taur Drúadan and tell him that you have covered many of the Rohirrim tracks in the Beacon Hills.\n",
[13214]="7004CE1F\n1\tTalk to Lorndúr\tLorndúr can be found in Loeglond. You should talk to Lorndúr\n2\tTalk to Thranduil\tKing Thranduil can be found within Felegoth. You should talk to Thranduil.\n",
[13215]="700217B5\n1\tBring the note to Gronu at his camp\tGronu can be found at his camp north of Harndirion, at the foot of the mountain. You should seek out Gronu and give him the message that you found.\n",
[13216]="70021A4A\n1\tDiscover the cavern and save the captives\tThe dungeon is behind the second waterfall, east of Gronu's camp. Gronu has asked you to find the dungeon where the Draig-lûth hold their prisoners and free his companions.\n2\tTalk to Gronu at his camp\tGronu is at his camp, west of the waterfall. You should return to Gronu and let him know that all of the captives that could be found have been freed.\n",
})
